  "question": {
    "text": "Let in&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;the coordinates of <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Internal angle bisector of <math><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and mid-point of <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Then, the ordinate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reflection of <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> about the line <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> which lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>The equation of <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;(line passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>)<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> is the point of intersection of <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>The point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence, the coordinates of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;(since, the mid point of&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>)</p>",
